WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.942 --> 00:00:03.860
- I was never raised to, uh, be a racist.

00:00:03.860 --> 00:00:08.114
It was never a part of my
life until I was in prison.

00:00:08.114 --> 00:00:11.487
It was born out of pure necessity.

00:00:11.487 --> 00:00:14.070
You have to change who you are.

00:00:17.902 --> 00:00:19.669
When you come into jail,
you come into prison,

00:00:19.669 --> 00:00:20.812
you've got your white gangs.

00:00:20.812 --> 00:00:22.259
You've got your black gangs.

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:23.365
If you step outside of that,

00:00:23.365 --> 00:00:25.252
you're not only gonna have one enemy,

00:00:25.252 --> 00:00:26.202
you're gonna have two.

00:00:26.202 --> 00:00:28.788
The tattoo for me was
definitely like a shield.

00:00:28.788 --> 00:00:32.110
The day I got released, I was
determined not to just give up

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:33.859
and say, "That's who I am."

00:00:33.859 --> 00:00:37.026
And I realized that I can change this.

00:00:39.795 --> 00:00:41.429
My name is Dave Cutlip,

00:00:41.429 --> 00:00:43.414
and we run Redemption Ink.

00:00:43.414 --> 00:00:45.885
I have been tattooing for over 20 years.

00:00:45.885 --> 00:00:48.125
We help people get a second chance

00:00:48.125 --> 00:00:51.875
by removing racist and
gang tattoos for free.

00:00:53.216 --> 00:00:55.691
We started about six months ago.

00:00:55.691 --> 00:00:57.858
I've done 16 coverups now.

00:00:58.772 --> 00:01:00.965
The demand for this,
to be honest with you,

00:01:00.965 --> 00:01:02.117
it's overwhelming.

00:01:02.117 --> 00:01:04.390
I'm gonna try and do it
at least once a week,

00:01:04.390 --> 00:01:06.725
either here or at conventions

00:01:06.725 --> 00:01:09.426
until I just can't tattoo anymore.

00:01:09.426 --> 00:01:13.774
People are just going
full-bore trying to get help.

00:01:13.774 --> 00:01:16.971
And most of them, I'd have to
say, they're already moved on.

00:01:16.971 --> 00:01:20.491
They just still have the tattoos
that are holding them back.

00:01:20.491 --> 00:01:22.268
Like, I'm glad that I have a talent

00:01:22.268 --> 00:01:24.409
that I can help somebody.

00:01:24.409 --> 00:01:27.640
Those people deserve the
pat on the back, not me.

00:01:27.640 --> 00:01:31.807
They did what they needed
to do to change their lives.

00:01:32.968 --> 00:01:33.801
- At the end of the day,

00:01:33.801 --> 00:01:35.727
I didn't want my daughter
picking up on that message.

00:01:35.727 --> 00:01:37.274
I didn't want my daughter thinking

00:01:37.274 --> 00:01:40.916
like that type of thinking is right.

00:01:40.916 --> 00:01:43.177
Or asking me where I
got it or why I got it.

00:01:43.177 --> 00:01:44.720
She doesn't have to see any of that.

00:01:44.720 --> 00:01:46.302
And I'm just like grateful
for that every day

00:01:46.302 --> 00:01:50.219
is that she never had to
see me as that person.

